        <name>nsight_export</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::gpu::GPUMetrics::nsight_export</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Export kernel records in CUDA Nsight Compute-compatible JSON. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Produces a JSON document that mirrors the top-level schema used by Nsight Compute&apos;s <computeroutput>--export json</computeroutput> option so that tooling built around that format (e.g. ncu-ui, custom analysis scripts) can consume the output without modification.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>UTF-8 JSON string. When no kernels have been recorded the <computeroutput>"Kernels"</computeroutput> array is present but empty (<computeroutput>"Kernels": []</computeroutput>). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
